NOTICE
======

This repository is a Go port of **muse2api**, an OpenAI-compatible proxy that
drives muse.ai through a headless Chromium instance controlled over CDP.

Upstream
--------

- Project: muse2api
- Repository: https://github.com/czg86389-hub/muse2api
- Upstream license: MIT (see `LICENSE`), copyright (c) 2026 MUSE2API Authors
- Ported baseline: upstream commit `42ee039` (version 1.5.4). The reference
  snapshots used while porting were taken from the deployed container running
  version 1.5.3 (`2374061`), then reconciled against 1.5.4.

What is derived from upstream
-----------------------------

- The injected JavaScript is reproduced verbatim from upstream `engine.py`.
  It is not hand-copied: `tools/gen_js.mjs` extracts it programmatically from
  the deployed source into `internal/engine/js.go`, and the golden
  `internal/engine/testdata/engine_js.json` records the rendered strings so the
  extraction itself is checked.
- The HTTP contract (routes, status codes, error shells, SSE framing, response
  key order, header behaviour) mirrors upstream `app.py` request for request.
- Golden files under `internal/*/testdata/` were **recorded from a running
  Python instance** rather than written by hand, and the Go tests replay them
  byte-for-byte. Recording scripts live in `tools/golden/`.
- `internal/webui/admin.html`, `internal/webui/assets/openapi.json` and
  `internal/webui/assets/oauth2-redirect.html` are byte-exact snapshots
  captured from the deployed upstream service, not re-implemented markup.

Intentional deviations
----------------------

The port is not byte-identical in behaviour. Every deviation is tagged
`DEVIATION:` at the place in the code where it happens, with a number (#1..#20)
that indexes the design note kept alongside this project (that note is
maintained locally and is not published in this repository — search the code
for `DEVIATION:` for the authoritative inline record). The main ones:

- Idle browser release plus opt-out of the keepalive warm tab, so an idle
  container stays in the single-digit MiB range (`MUSE2API_BROWSER_IDLE_MINUTES`,
  `MUSE2API_WARM_TAB`).
- No in-container git self-update: `/admin/repo/pull`, `/admin/repo/push` and
  `/admin/update/upgrade` report the version and the manual steps instead.
- `/openapi.json` and the admin panel are embedded snapshots rather than
  generated at runtime; a test reconciles the route table against the
  document so drift fails loudly.

Operational notes before publishing
-----------------------------------

- Nothing here contains credentials. Deployment host, user and password are
  read from the environment by `tools/nas_deploy.mjs` and
  `tools/golden/run_on_nas.mjs` (`NAS_HOST`, `NAS_USER`, `NAS_PW`) and are
  never written to the repository.
- Recorded secrets in goldens are redacted (`<REDACTED>`), cookie values in
  engine goldens are fakes (`s`, `g`, `NEWVML`), and client addresses in the
  access-log golden are replaced with RFC 5737 documentation addresses.
- The upstream Python source used as the porting reference is deliberately
  excluded via `.gitignore` (`.reference/`) and is not part of this repository.

